  "readme": [
    {
      "section": "dsh-weather",
      "text": "Weather forecast for the DeepSeek Harness web GUI. A draggable floating weather card in the bottom-right corner, plus a model-callable `weather` tool — with playful easter eggs. Weather data comes from [Open-Meteo](https://open-meteo.com/) (free, no API key)."
    },
    {
      "section": "Features",
      "text": "- **Floating weather card** — a ☀️ button in the bottom-right opens a draggable card showing current conditions and a 3-day forecast.\n- **Auto-locate by IP** — on first open, the card locates your city from your IP and resolves a Chinese name (e.g. 南京); it falls back to 北京 if that fails.\n- **Search any city** — Chinese or English names, e.g. 北京 / 上海 / New York / Tokyo.\n- **Model tool** — the agent answers \"北京明天天气\" / \"上海要带伞吗\" by calling the `weather` tool directly.\n- **Easter eggs** 🍬 — weather one-liners (sunny = \"宜摸鱼忌加班\", ≥35° = \"出门五分钟流汗两小时\") and city-specific jokes (`南极` = \"企鹅比人多，出门记得带鱼\").\n- **Theme-aware** — uses Harness design tokens, so it follows light/dark mode."
    },
    {
      "section": "Install",
      "text": "```sh\ndsh plugin --profile web add https://github.com/XCKjacksparrow/dsh-weather/archive/refs/tags/v0.1.0.tar.gz\n```\n\nThen restart `dsh web` so the Host and the browser client load the plugin."
    },
    {
      "section": "Install from a local build",
      "text": "```sh\nnpm run build\nnpm pack\ndsh plugin --profile web add ./dsh-weather-0.1.0.tgz\n```"
    },
    {
      "section": "Usage",
      "text": "- Click the ☀️ button in the bottom-right, type a city, and press Enter or **查询**.\n- Ask the agent anything weather-related, e.g. \"上海明天要带伞吗？\""
    },
    {
      "section": "Development",
      "text": "```sh\nnpm install\nnpm run build   # build host + client bundles into lib/\nnpm test        # run the unit tests (node --test)\n```\n\nBuilt files under `lib/` are committed, so installing the plugin does not require a build step."
    },
    {
      "section": "Data sources",
      "text": "- Weather: [Open-Meteo](https://open-meteo.com/) — free, no API key.\n- IP geolocation: `api.ipapi.is` (primary), then `get.geojs.io` and `ipwho.is` (fallbacks).\n- Chinese reverse geocoding: BigDataCloud.\n\n> Privacy: the widget sends your IP to a third-party geolocation service once, on first open, to infer an approximate city. Nothing is stored."
    },
    {
      "section": "Configuration",
      "text": "No configuration required."
    },
    {
      "section": "License",
      "text": "MIT"
    }
  ],
